     "medium": "Wool tapestry",
     "form": "Textile",
     "style": "Modern British",
     "summary": "Behind the high altar of the new Coventry Cathedral, built beside the ruins of the medieval cathedral destroyed by bombing in 1940, Christ sits enthroned in a vast green field. He is enclosed in a mandorla and surrounded by the four living creatures of the Apocalypse that stand for the Evangelists. Below him, Sutherland placed a small Crucifixion, joining the Christ of the Passion to the Christ of glory in a single image of hope after war.",
